  "text": "Venus soaks up less sunlight than Earth does, and it's the hottest planet in the solar system. It gets almost twice our sunlight, but its bright clouds bounce three-quarters of it away. The air is thick carbon dioxide, 90 times heavier than ours, 465 degrees. The full film, What Happened to Venus?",
